{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZqonfzH7jX33J1dEvBa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I have enough information. Let me now provide the findings from the ANALYSIS phase:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — currently has create, getById, and list endpoints with no confirm capability\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — provides save/findById/existsById operations using ConcurrentHashMap\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — defines ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum with existing codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29` — central exception handling returning ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions in this repository:**\n1. Exceptions: ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) are thrown by controllers; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError responses\n2. Status codes: 201 CREATED for POST creating new resources; 200 OK implied for other responses\n3. HTTP verbs: @PostMapping for create/action endpoints, @GetMapping for read endpoints\n4. Response types: ResponseEntity<T> for POSTs with explicit status, direct object return for GETs\n5. Error codes: Closed set in ErrorCode enum; each failure type has a specific code\n6. Testing: Spring Boot integration tests with MockMvc, jsonPath assertions for response validation\n\n**Affected files:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — must add the confirm endpoint (cannot avoid)\n- `ApiError.kt` — must add error code for \"shipment cannot be confirmed\" state conflict (follows existing pattern)\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for the new endpoint (required by ticket acceptance criteria)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency: confirm twice must succeed; the implementation must handle CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED correctly\n- State validation: must reject CANCELLED shipments with 409, not treat them as success\n- Error code proliferation: adding error codes changes the API contract\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What should the error code be named for rejecting a CANCELLED shipment? I'll use `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` following the semantic pattern.\n\nNow I move to DESIGN.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the ErrorCode enum to represent state conflicts during confirmation.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the shipment by ID (throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND if not found)\n   - Checks if status is CANCELLED (throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED if it is)\n   - Sets status to CONFIRMED (idempotent: if already CONFIRMED, this has no effect)\n   - Saves and returns the shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without changing state (idempotency)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Creating a separate `ShipmentService` class: Rejected because the existing codebase uses thin controllers with repository calls directly, not a service layer. Adding a service would be unnecessary refactoring outside the ticket scope.\n- Using an existing error code like VALIDATION_FAILED: Rejected because the error is not a validation failure; it's a state conflict. Adding a specific code is more useful for clients and matches the existing pattern (compare SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND vs generic 404).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | HTTP | Via |\n|------|------|-------|------|-----|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById | repository.save with CONFIRMED status | 200 OK | ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById | repository.save (idempotent, no change) | 200 OK | ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| Unknown shipment | repository.findById returns null | nothing | 404 | ResourceNotFoundException |\n| CANCELLED → reject | repository.findById | nothing | 409 | ConflictException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: Confirm CREATED shipment** — Create shipment S-1, confirm it, verify response is 200 OK with status CONFIRMED\n2. **Test: Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment** — Create shipment S-2, confirm it, confirm again, verify both succeed and status remains CONFIRMED\n3. **Test: Reject CANCELLED shipment** — Create and manually save a CANCELLED shipment, attempt to confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n4. **Test: Reject unknown shipment** — Attempt to confirm non-existent shipment, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1039,"cache_read_input_tokens":16906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1039},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6a9034b-b7e3-411d-87d0-5f4423e4a20c","uuid":"8a94fe16-dbc7-4747-8212-670091edfc0d","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:14:43.416Z","request_id":"req_011CfZqonHfbZDx8q7dRrfdE"}
